+description: "Give Hermes a computer: hand tasks that need a screen (web apps behind a login, admin consoles, desktop software, forms with no import) to Sai, Simular's computer-use agent, which does them on a cloud computer Simular hosts and reports back in text. Agent Plugins v1 package (plugin.json + mcp.json + skills/), configuration only; the MCP server runs as npx @simular-ai/sai-mcp@0.4.0 over stdio, so Node.js 22.12+ and npm are required. Needs a Sai API key (from platform.simular.ai), set in Settings > Plugins or as SAI_API_KEY in the profile .env. Disclosure — Runs the npm package @simular-ai/sai-mcp@0.4.0 through npx; every task, its results and the SAI_API_KEY go to api.simular.ai and spend the account's Sai credit or free computer time; the agent can upload any local file it chooses (up to 25 MB) to Simular with sai_upload, run code on the Simular cloud computer (sai_control_exec), and approve Sai's own permission requests, without a Hermes prompt; a local task view is served on 127.0.0.1 with a per-run token, and sai_live_link returns a link that lets whoever holds it control the cloud computer until it expires."
